},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"readonly "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"object"},{"type":"text","value":"[]"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":" array received from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatParamsFromRequest(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatParamsFromRequestBody(...)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"returns-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/MergedAgentTools.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MergedAgentTools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TServerTools"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A merged array suitable for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ tools })"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"call-signature","text":"Call Signature","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":3},{"id":"tservertools","text":"TServerTools","level":4},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":3},{"id":"servertools","text":"serverTools","level":4},{"id":"clienttools","text":"clientTools","level":4},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":3},{"id":"call-signature-2","text":"Call Signature","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters-2","text":"Type Parameters","level":3},{"id":"tservertools-2","text":"TServerTools","level":4},{"id":"parameters-2","text":"Parameters","level":3},{"id":"servertools-2","text":"serverTools","level":4},{"id":"clienttools-2","text":"clientTools","level":4},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## Call Signature\n\n```ts\nfunction mergeAgentTools<TServerTools>(serverTools, clientTools): TServerTools;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/utilities/chat-params.ts:355](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/utilities/chat-params.ts#L355)\n\nMerge a server-side tool array with the AG-UI client-declared tools\nreceived in the request body.\n\nRules:\n- Server tools win on name collision. The client's declaration is\n  ignored if the server already has a tool with that name. The client's\n  UI-side handler still fires when the streamed tool-result event comes\n  through (see `chat-client.ts` `onToolCall`), giving the\n  \"after server execution the client also handles\" semantic for free.\n- Client-only tools (name not in `serverTools`) become no-execute\n  entries: the runtime's existing `ClientToolRequest` path handles\n  them — server emits a tool-call request, client executes via its\n  registered handler, client posts back the result.\n\nTyping:\n- Empty `clientTools` preserves the server tuple (closed name union).\n- Non-empty `clientTools` returns a widened array that honestly includes\n  client stubs, so the merged array does not claim a closed server-only\n  name union.\n\n### Type Parameters\n\n#### TServerTools\n\n`TServerTools` *extends* readonly [`AnyTool`](../type-aliases/AnyTool.md)[]\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### serverTools\n\n`TServerTools`\n\nThe server's tool array (e.g. from\n  `[myToolDef.server(...)]`). Pass directly to `chat({ tools })`.\n\n#### clientTools\n\nreadonly \\[\\]\n\nThe `tools` array received from\n  `chatParamsFromRequest(...)` / `chatParamsFromRequestBody(...)`.\n\n### Returns\n\n`TServerTools`\n\nA merged array suitable for `chat({ tools })`.\n\n## Call Signature\n\n```ts\nfunction mergeAgentTools<TServerTools>(serverTools, clientTools): MergedAgentTools<TServerTools>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/utilities/chat-params.ts:358](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/utilities/chat-params.ts#L358)\n\nMerge a server-side tool array with the AG-UI client-declared tools\nreceived in the request body.\n\nRules:\n- Server tools win on name collision. The client's declaration is\n  ignored if the server already has a tool with that name. The client's\n  UI-side handler still fires when the streamed tool-result event comes\n  through (see `chat-client.ts` `onToolCall`), giving the\n  \"after server execution the client also handles\" semantic for free.\n- Client-only tools (name not in `serverTools`) become no-execute\n  entries: the runtime's existing `ClientToolRequest` path handles\n  them — server emits a tool-call request, client executes via its\n  registered handler, client posts back the result.\n\nTyping:\n- Empty `clientTools` preserves the server tuple (closed name union).\n- Non-empty `clientTools` returns a widened array that honestly includes\n  client stubs, so the merged array does not claim a closed server-only\n  name union.\n\n### Type Parameters\n\n#### TServerTools\n\n`TServerTools` *extends* readonly [`AnyTool`](../type-aliases/AnyTool.md)[]\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### serverTools\n\n`TServerTools`\n\nThe server's tool array (e.g. from\n  `[myToolDef.server(...)]`). Pass directly to `chat({ tools })`.\n\n#### clientTools\n\nreadonly `object`[]\n\nThe `tools` array received from\n  `chatParamsFromRequest(...)` / `chatParamsFromRequestBody(...)`.\n\n### Returns\n\n[`MergedAgentTools`](../type-aliases/MergedAgentTools.md)\\<`TServerTools`\\>\n\nA merged array suitable for `chat({ tools })`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: mergeAgentTools\ntitle: mergeAgentTools\n---\n\n## Call Signature\n\n```ts\nfunction mergeAgentTools<TServerTools>(serverTools, clientTools): TServerTools;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/utilities/chat-params.ts:355](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/utilities/chat-params.ts#L355)\n\nMerge a server-side tool array with the AG-UI client-declared tools\nreceived in the request body.\n\nRules:\n- Server tools win on name collision. The client's declaration is\n  ignored if the server already has a tool with that name. The client's\n  UI-side handler still fires when the streamed tool-result event comes\n  through (see `chat-client.ts` `onToolCall`), giving the\n  \"after server execution the client also handles\" semantic for free.\n- Client-only tools (name not in `serverTools`) become no-execute\n  entries: the runtime's existing `ClientToolRequest` path handles\n  them — server emits a tool-call request, client executes via its\n  registered handler, client posts back the result.\n\nTyping:\n- Empty `clientTools` preserves the server tuple (closed name union).\n- Non-empty `clientTools` returns a widened array that honestly includes\n  client stubs, so the merged array does not claim a closed server-only\n  name union.\n\n### Type Parameters\n\n#### TServerTools\n\n`TServerTools` *extends* readonly [`AnyTool`](../type-aliases/AnyTool.md)[]\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### serverTools\n\n`TServerTools`\n\nThe server's tool array (e.g. from\n  `[myToolDef.server(...)]`). Pass directly to `chat({ tools })`.\n\n#### clientTools\n\nreadonly \\[\\]\n\nThe `tools` array received from\n  `chatParamsFromRequest(...)` / `chatParamsFromRequestBody(...)`.\n\n### Returns\n\n`TServerTools`\n\nA merged array suitable for `chat({ tools })`.\n\n## Call Signature\n\n```ts\nfunction mergeAgentTools<TServerTools>(serverTools, clientTools): MergedAgentTools<TServerTools>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/utilities/chat-params.ts:358](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/utilities/chat-params.ts#L358)\n\nMerge a server-side tool array with the AG-UI client-declared tools\nreceived in the request body.\n\nRules:\n- Server tools win on name collision. The client's declaration is\n  ignored if the server already has a tool with that name. The client's\n  UI-side handler still fires when the streamed tool-result event comes\n  through (see `chat-client.ts` `onToolCall`), giving the\n  \"after server execution the client also handles\" semantic for free.\n- Client-only tools (name not in `serverTools`) become no-execute\n  entries: the runtime's existing `ClientToolRequest` path handles\n  them — server emits a tool-call request, client executes via its\n  registered handler, client posts back the result.\n\nTyping:\n- Empty `clientTools` preserves the server tuple (closed name union).\n- Non-empty `clientTools` returns a widened array that honestly includes\n  client stubs, so the merged array does not claim a closed server-only\n  name union.\n\n### Type Parameters\n\n#### TServerTools\n\n`TServerTools` *extends* readonly [`AnyTool`](../type-aliases/AnyTool.md)[]\n\n### Parameters\n\n#### serverTools\n\n`TServerTools`\n\nThe server's tool array (e.g. from\n  `[myToolDef.server(...)]`). Pass directly to `chat({ tools })`.\n\n#### clientTools\n\nreadonly `object`[]\n\nThe `tools` array received from\n  `chatParamsFromRequest(...)` / `chatParamsFromRequestBody(...)`.\n\n### Returns\n\n[`MergedAgentTools`](../type-aliases/MergedAgentTools.md)\\<`TServerTools`\\>\n\nA merged array suitable for `chat({ tools })`.\n"}
